Patchlevel 3, upgrading NetHack to version 3.1.3, was submitted to
comp.sources.games for distribution.  We were adviced by the moderator
of c.s.g. not to expect the distribution before Monday.

Soon after the distribution of Patchlevel 2, a deadly bug was discovered
in the Mac port, other bugs were also discovered in the Amiga port, in
the VMS port, and in the game's main code.  This is the reason why no
official binaries were made available.  Of course, we didn't expect that
it will take us this long to fix all these bugs.

The NetHack 3.1.3 binaries will be distributed to their usual archives,
and will be posted on linc.cis.upenn.edu as soon as our various porting
groups finish preparing and testing their binary packages.

Patchlevel 3, while primarily a bug fixing patch, does include some enhance-
ments:

Mac windowing was further revised, and the Macintosh code was ported to
Think C by Barton House.  Amiga windowing was also touched up.

The MSDOS black/gray/white intensities were changed again to avoid
confusing displays on some PC hardware.  New video options were added
to allow configuration around any other oddities.

Bugs were fixed.  In particular, an elusive bug dealing with horns of
plenty was finally found, along with a couple VMS-specific ones such as
fetching some bones files.  A number of messages were revised and updated
as well.

Bones files and saved NetHack 3.1.2 games will NOT work with NetHack 3.1.3.
Please delete them when you upgrade your code, to avoid problems.

We read rec.games.hack carefully and attentively, but please make sure to
also send copies of your bug reports to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu, the
official address of the development team.  We thank the many people who did
send us bug reports and suggestions for improvements.  Enjoy.

For the NetHack development team,

-Izchak


